Mind, though, that Grimtooth is a dagger, priests are restricted in
daggers, and if the artifact gets granted from a sacrifice a priest
can only become Basic in it. Priests are also restricted in knifes,
so a crysknife might also not be the best thing (at first glance).
But the crysknife has a +3 to hit bonus which might be crucial in
case you have to rely on a [initially] restricted weapon, at least
until you can get to Basic the crysknife seems to be better. But the
(+1) mace gives (at Basic) 5.5/4.5 damage, and priests can advance
the proficiency here. Usually you also get your artifacts or a worm
tooth not too early in the game. Therefore, for a priest, I consider
the mace to be preferable to Grimtooth or crysknife. (A drawback is
only that it is corrodable, while the granted artifact or crysknife
does not corrode, which is an advantage if meleeing careless.)

